model g11_where_hole
  tally 2
  on 2026-03-15
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-03-31
  note "T, issue #41, G11: the steps an adjustment is measured at (E §5 steps 1-4) are the versions known after the instance's day and by the cut: a move bound over a kind of things whose where is a hole for one member (bob), known for another (ana) and false for a third (cid), with a version known exactly on the instances' day and none after it, so no step measures them."

source fixture "T's fixture for S's kernel tests (invented values)"

unit PLN: currency minor 0.01

kind member

place konto: accounts PLN lives 2025-01-01..

place world: outside lives 2025-01-01..

input active[p in member]: bool question "Is the member active?"

input pay_day: date

input fee: money PLN

input late: money PLN

move dues[p in member on pay_day where active[p]]: transfers
  on pay_day
  leg cash from konto to world amount fee

ask q_bal: bal(konto, 2026-02-09), bal(konto, 2026-02-28) law cut

ask q_flows: flows(dues, 2026-02-01 .. 2026-02-28) law cut

version facts
  cite fixture
  governs always
  known 2025-12-01
  member + [ana, bob, cid] lives 2025-01-01..
  active[ana] = true "ana pays"
  active[cid] = false "cid doesn't; bob's is a hole"
  pay_day = 2026-02-10
  fee = 10.00
  opening[konto] = 100 at 2026-01-01 start

version on_the_day
  cite fixture
  governs always
  known 2026-02-10
  late = 1.00 "a version known on the instances' day"


